    "r_counts": {
      "source": "census-ALL.csv filtered to R-side ext (R, r, Rmd, rmd, qmd, Rnw, S, Rproj), then GATE's own job definition applied: drop is_template==TRUE and naming=='template'.",
      "why_the_filter_matters": "32,226 of 38,282 R rows for taxonomy prefixes are TEMPLATES, not jobs -- 84%. Counting them inflates every prefix and produced R_studies > total_studies, which is how the error was caught.",
      "r_jobs_definition": "distinct (study, prefix, folder, stem) tuples, matching job_census()'s n_jobs.",
      "closes": "the lower bound stated in inst/templates/README.md, whose R counts read .qmd only. Published there: ac 4, hz 3, hp 3, bh 2, hm 1, hs 1. Measured across all R extensions: ac 16, hz 5, hp 16, bh 2, hm 2, hs 7.",
